     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear unmarked users,</div><div><br></div><div>I`m using the colext function to understand the impact of hurricane Maria on birds and frogs distribution in Puerto Rico. </div><div><br></div><div>I`m working with 68 sampling sites in three transects along an elevational gradient (~75-1030meters), three primary visits (years), and 17 secondary occasions.</div><div><br></div><div>To estimate the rate of change in occupancy (<span style=\"font-family:NewPXMI_gnu;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">𝜆)</span> I`m using the derived parameter &quot;prime lambda&quot; <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:NewPXMI_gnu\">𝜆</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:5pt\">′ </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxmiaX\">= </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:NewPXMI_gnu\">𝜓</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:-3pt\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:NewPXMI;vertical-align:-3pt\">𝑡</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:-3pt\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:TeXGyrePagellaX;vertical-align:-3pt\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:-3pt\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">/</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:TeXGyrePagellaX\">1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">− </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:NewPXMI_gnu\">𝜓</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:-3pt\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:NewPXMI;vertical-align:-3pt\">𝑡</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:-3pt\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:TeXGyrePagellaX;vertical-align:-3pt\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:pxsys;vertical-align:-3pt\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">)/(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:NewPXMI_gnu\">𝜓</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:NewPXMI;vertical-align:-3pt\">𝑡</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">/</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:TeXGyrePagellaX\">1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">− </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:NewPXMI_gnu\">𝜓</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:7pt;font-family:NewPXMI;vertical-align:-3pt\">𝑡</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10pt;font-family:pxsys\">))</span></div><div><br></div><div>I`m calculating these values by hand with the smoothed values from the nonparboot  function on my best model for each species.</div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to obtain the SE for this derivated parameter in unmarked?</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks</div><div><br></div><div>Best</div><div><br></div><div>Marconi</div></div>"
